    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d307">

                <pb facs="0306" n="294" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg294"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/8733: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-03T12:00:00+03:00">March 3,
                            1941—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>418. <hi rendition="#italic">Pravda</hi> this morning publishes the first report
                    which has appeared in the Soviet press of the entrance of German troops into
                    Bulgaria. The announcement is not prominently headlined, is very brief, and
                    there is no Soviet comment. It takes the form of a Tass item from Berlin dated
                    March 2 as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The DNB<anchor n="56" xml:id="d307-f1"/> reports from Sofia that German
                            troops have entered the territory of Bulgaria with the consent of the
                            Bulgarian Government.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d307-f1" n="56" xml:id="d307-f1-content">
                <p>Deutsches Nachrichten Büro.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
